<%# == WHICH FILES of one area moved — the rung below the panel above
        The panel above ranks AREAS by how far their example count moved and, until this existed,
        stopped there: its directory cell was inert text, so the one question a row like
        `spec/models 412 → 459 (+47)` provokes had no answer on this page or on any other. Nothing
        in the application read growth at the file grain at all.

        "Heaviest spec files" could not stand in, for the reason `SpecDirectoryDurations` gives
        about its own rollup: that list is a run-wide top ten ranked by DURATION, so an area that
        gained forty-seven FAST examples has not one of its rows in it. The panel that sees the
        movement cannot see the files; the panel that sees files cannot see the movement.

        Its subject is the doubt the caption above discloses and cannot resolve — a MOVED test is
        the same test, so a relocation reads there as one area growing and another shrinking with
        nothing added and nothing deleted. This panel does not resolve it either and asserts nothing
        new: it counts rows per FILE per run, pairs no example with any other example, and puts the
        operands where a HUMAN can read the difference. `user_spec.rb` at "New file" beside
        `legacy_user_spec.rb` at "File removed" is a rename at a glance; two files at `+47` and
        `−47` are not.

        Reached by the SAME `?spec_directory=` ask the durations drill-down reads, so one ask opens
        EVERY panel that reads it over one area, each answering in its own grain. Intended, and how
        `drill_down_path` composes asks.

        It renders ONLY where the panel above is comparable, and that is not a nicety: a drill-in
        that compared two runs the panel it hangs off refuses to compare would assert, in a closer
        view, a comparison the wider view has just withheld. `SpecDirectoryFileGrowth` inherits that
        verdict rather than re-deriving it — two of its six states are facts about a RUN and are
        not derivable from one area's rows at all.

        No "Close directory" of its own. `?spec_directory=` is ONE ask with one exit, and that exit
        already exists on "Spec files in this directory" above, the panel that owns the gesture. A
        second button clearing the same ask would be two ways out of one state and a further row in
        the carry-through matrix that duplicates an existing cell.

        Same visibility rule and same gate as the panels around it: read-only suite telemetry on
        `current_repository(:view)`, outside `manage_keys`, and nothing here widens that. %>
<% if @spec_directory_file_growth&.comparable? %>
      <%= render UI::PanelComponent.new(title: "Files that grew or shrank in this directory",
                                        id: "spec-directory-file-growth", class: "rc-drill") do %>
        <% if @spec_directory_file_growth.recorded? && @spec_directory_file_growth.any_movement? %>
          <%= render UI::NoteComponent.new(summary: "How to read this", id: "spec-directory-file-growth-basis") do %>
            <span class="font-mono text-app-content-secondary"><%= @spec_directory_file_growth.path %></span>
            —
            <% if @spec_directory_file_growth.truncated? %>
              the <%= number_with_delimiter(@spec_directory_file_growth.rows.size) %> spec files that
              moved most, of the
              <%= number_with_delimiter(@spec_directory_file_growth.file_count) %> either run
              recorded in this area — largest movement first, in both directions
            <% else %>
              all <%= number_with_delimiter(@spec_directory_file_growth.file_count) %>
              <%= "spec file".pluralize(@spec_directory_file_growth.file_count) %> either run
              recorded in this area — largest movement first, in both directions
            <% end %>
            — measured between this run and
            <span class="font-mono"><%= @previous_test_run.commit_sha.first(7) %></span>, the
            previous run on this branch.
            <% if @spec_directory_file_growth.any_unmoved? %>
              Where the movement runs out before the list does, files that did not move are listed
              too, as ±0.
            <% end %>
            A file listed as new beside one listed as removed is what a RENAMED or relocated file
            looks like from here — and so is a real addition beside a real deletion. This panel
            counts each run's rows and pairs no example with any other example, so it cannot tell
            the two apart and does not try; both files are named so a reader can.
            This area is the immediate parent of the files listed, so a nested area such as a
            subdirectory of it is its own area rather than part of this list.
            Counted off the
            <%= number_with_delimiter(@spec_directory_file_growth.previous_recorded_count) %> and
            <%= number_with_delimiter(@spec_directory_file_growth.latest_recorded_count) %> example
            rows the two runs recorded in this area — this area's own rows, not the suite totals the
            panel above is counted over and not the suite size on the Summary.
          <% end %>
          <%= render UI::TableComponent.new(
                columns: ["Spec file", { label: "Examples then", end: true }, { label: "Examples now", end: true }, { label: "Change", end: true }],
                describedby: "spec-directory-file-growth-basis", sortable: true) do %>
            <% @spec_directory_file_growth.rows.each do |file| %>
              <tr>
                <td class="font-mono text-xs [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">
                  <% if file.removed_file? %><%= file.path %><% else %>
                    <%= link_to file.path, drill_down_path(@repository, spec_file: file.path, spec_directory: @spec_directory_file_growth.path, anchor: "slow"),
                                class: "rc-link", aria: { current: file.path == @spec_file_request ? "true" : nil } %>
                  <% end %>
                </td>
                <td class="num mute" data-sort="<%= file.previous_count %>"><%= file.previous_count_label %></td>
                <td class="num mute" data-sort="<%= file.latest_count %>"><%= file.latest_count_label %></td>
                <td class="num" data-sort="<%= file.change %>" aria-label="<%= file.change_reading %>"><%= delta_tag(file.change_label, tone: file.change.zero? ? :flat : :info) %></td>
              </tr>
            <% end %>
          <% end %>
        <% elsif @spec_directory_file_growth.recorded? %>
          <%= render UI::EmptyStateComponent.new(
                title: "No file moved",
                description: "Every one of the " \
                             "#{number_with_delimiter(@spec_directory_file_growth.file_count)} " \
                             "#{'spec file'.pluralize(@spec_directory_file_growth.file_count)} " \
                             "either run recorded in #{@spec_directory_file_growth.path} holds the " \
                             "same number of examples in both, so nothing in this area grew or " \
                             "shrank between them."
              ) %>
        <% else %>
          <%= render UI::EmptyStateComponent.new(
                title: "No spec files in this directory",
                description: "Neither this run nor the previous run on this branch recorded any " \
                             "examples in #{@spec_directory_file_growth.path}. It may have been " \
                             "renamed or deleted before both of them, or never have run in either " \
                             "— the “Areas that grew or shrank” table lists the areas whose " \
                             "example count moved most between the two."
              ) %>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
